2. Stressors 
Purpose: 
Define what pressures or distortions are being introduced. 
Examples of stress dimensions (structure only): 
• Time pressure; 
• Conflicting telemetry; 
• Stakeholder demand; 
• Ambiguous definitions; 
• Delegation ambiguity; 
Stressors simulate pressure on reasoning, not system failure.

3. Context Notes 
Purpose: 
Explain why this simulation is being run. 
This is narrative context. 
It should clarify: 
• What kind of governance behavior is being explored 
• That the purpose is exploratory 
• That no adequacy determination is being made 
Example: 
Baseline stress test of AI usage percentage reporting under 
operational pressure to identify fragility in scope boundaries, signal 
interpretation, and escalation triggers without making adequacy or 
compliance determinations.

